# DTF tier manifest: multi-replica-cold-boot  (artifact-keeper#5601 / #5993)
# Profile-set: filesystem + topology.three-replica-cold (three replicas on one
# database, each with restart: on-failure). The oracle stops all three,
# recreates an empty database and starts the three at the same moment, so
# the stack's own `up --wait` is never part of the race.
#
# THE BUG (#5601, #5993; fixed by #5999 in 1.12.0)
# On a fresh database with several replicas starting together, the replica
# holding the migration lock runs a non-transactional CREATE INDEX
# CONCURRENTLY. The index build waits for every transaction with an older
# snapshot, including the other replicas, which blocked in
# pg_advisory_lock() inside a statement. Postgres broke the cycle by aborting
# one side with 40P01 deadlock detected; the losing pod exited and restarted
# 1-2 times before the install converged. #5999 makes waiting replicas poll
# pg_try_advisory_lock() between statements (no snapshot held while they
# wait) and repairs any INVALID index a lost build left behind.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1). A regression pin: green on 1.12.0
# and later (every CONCURRENTLY migration up to the image's newest, 417 on
# 1.13.0), red on 1.11.x (5 restarts in 3 replicas on 1.11.11, measured).
#   (FIX)        none of the three replicas restarted (RestartCount 0) and no
#                replica log has "deadlock detected".
#   (FIX)        the database has no INVALID index.
#   (CONTROL)    all three replicas answer /readyz 200, each logged
#                "Database migrations complete", and every migration in the
#                ledger succeeded.
COVERS="5601"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem topology.three-replica-cold"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
